// Reference only -- not processed by any tool (no idlc yet, Phase 4).
// observer_attach is bidirectional, so unlike the other three
// examples' client.idl (which only ever calls an interface), this
// one both implements and calls: the observer implements Observer
// (what the subject calls back) but is itself a client of Subject
// (what it calls once, to attach).
#include "observer_attach.idl"

// Implements: one HaceExamples::Observer object, under object key
// "obsv", on UDP port 59132, so the subject has a known, stable
// address to call back on. update(event) is dispatched as a oneway
// call -- no reply is ever sent.
//
// Calls: HaceExamples::Subject::attach(self) once, as a genuine
// twoway call (passing its own IOR, CDR-encoded, as the request
// argument) against the subject's "subj" object on UDP port 59131.
//
// Implemented identically by c/observer_client.c,
// rust/src/observer_client.rs, and
// ada95/{observer_impl,observer_client}.adb.
